{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DOMRange","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a DOM Range object, the startContainer + startOffset tuple represents the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point. Similarly, the the endContainer + endOffset tuple represents the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" boundary point."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In both cases, the start\/endContainer property is a pointer to either a DOM text node, or a DOM"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element (this typically depends on the mechanism from which the DOM Range instance originates,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for example when obtaining the currently-selected document fragment using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"window.selection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API). In the case of a DOM text node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position within the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"character data. In the case of a DOM element node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that designates a child text node."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"text":" field is optional. When only the start field is specified, the domRange object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"represents a “collapsed” range that has identical ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"text":" boundary points.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"https:\/\/github.com\/readium\/architecture\/blob\/master\/models\/locators\/extensions\/html.md#the-domrange-object"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/readiumshared\/domrange"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This construct enables a serializable representation of a DOM Range."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DOMRange","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DOMRange","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"ReadiumShared"}],"title":"DOMRange","externalID":"s:13ReadiumShared8DOMRangeV","role":"symbol"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Point"]},{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(json:warnings:)","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(start:end:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/jsonObject"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONObjectEncodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONValueDecodable-Implementati